# Language classification (github/linguist)
#
# AIOrc is a TypeScript backend. The vanilla HTML pages under public/ are large
# enough to outweigh it in GitHub's language stats, which pushes the repository
# out of TypeScript searches and filters. The rules below exclude what is not
# hand-written backend or frontend source, so the classification reflects what
# the project actually is.

# The vanilla pages: markup with inline styles and scripts, not the source of
# record for any logic. Excluded from stats, still diffed normally.
public/*.html linguist-documentation
public/project.html.legacy linguist-documentation

# Vite output. Built by `npm run build:flow` from src-frontend/ into public/.
# Linguist already skips minified files, but declaring it keeps the stats stable
# if the bundle ever ships unminified.
public/flow-editor.js linguist-generated
public/flow-editor.css linguist-generated

# Deliberately NOT excluded:
#   src-frontend/  — first-party TypeScript and TSX (the React Flow editor).
#                    It is the source the bundle is built from, it counts as
#                    TypeScript, and excluding it would lower the very total
#                    this file exists to raise.
#   public/*.css, public/info-modal.js, public/ui-dialogs.js
#                  — hand-written, small, and honest to count.

# Normalize line endings for text files.
* text=auto
